            <div xml:id="d18">

                <pb facs="0123" n="17" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg17"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Duke de Arcos.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-08-05"><hi rendition="#small-caps">August</hi> 5,
                        1901</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your personal note of the 30th ultimo to Doctor Hill, Assistant Secretary of
                    State, in which you advise him that your Government is disposed to conclude by
                    an exchange of notes the agreement (suggested in your memorandum of April 18
                    last and this department’s of June 5 last) for the purpose of dispensing with
                    the authentication of signatures affixed to letters rogatory issuing from
                    Spanish courts to those of Porto Rico and the Philippines, and from the courts
                    of Porto Rico and the Philippines to those of Spain, if the letters rogatory
                    shall be transmitted through the diplomatic channel.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to quote the memoranda exchanged as follows:</p>



